                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 7,
                "retweet_count": 13,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Last year, I pushed back against a sweetheart deal that gave Doma Holdings, a politically connected company,  a no-bid contract to run FHFA\u2019s title insurance pilot program. The program was then rescinded\u2026.until this year's State of the Union when President Biden announced this revival of the pilot.\n\nEarlier this week, I wrote to the SEC regarding unusual trading activity surrounding Doma Holdings, which went from the brink of bankruptcy to merging with one of the largest title Insurers in the country thanks to a sweetheart deal from the Biden Administration.\n\nOur federal government must not be leveraged to enrich the political allies of the administration. The SEC must investigate immediately. \n\nSee my letter here:",
                "text_lang": "en",
